; Regions of two rings which meet without one being inside the other, and the
; arrangements either side of them.
;
; The counter is the shape this fixture is for: a four-metre square with a
; four-by-two return along one side of it, abutting it along part of a wall and
; meeting it at a corner. The two rings are the same two rings in every one of
; the four nodes which reference them, and the loops differ only in which of
; the return's corners the edge list is written from and which way round it
; runs. Twenty-four square metres is a property of the shape, so all four
; measure twenty-four.

; The counter body: four metres square, sixteen square metres.
(vertex geom:V-01
  (label "Counter body, corner 1")
  (frame frame:building)
  (position
    (value (4.0 0.0 0.0) m)
    (source "Interior control set IC-01, Acme Surveys")
    (method method:total-station)
    (accuracy (independent 0.004 m) (systematic 0.008 m control:CP-3))
    (date "2026-02-18")))
