; Two rings which overlap from a shared corner: an L-shaped counter drawn as its
; two runs, four by one and one by four, which overlap in the one-by-one square
; at the inside of the L. The runs share the corner at the top of the L and part
; of the side either side of it, so every corner and every midpoint of each run
; is on the other's boundary or outside it — which is what let the pair read as
; beside one another and be summed, with the overlap counted twice: eight square
; metres, which is not the union's seven nor the area of anything else. The pair
; is named, just as the crossing plates above are.
